lation\": \"quantized_from\", \"extensions\": {\"notes\": \"The report describes text pretraining, large-scale distillation, reasoning/tool-use post-training, and MXFP4 post-training quantization, but does not identify a specific predecessor checkpoint or distillation teacher. The relation records the disclosed quantization step; no unnamed checkpoint is asserted as an input.\", \"disclosure_status\": \"partially_disclosed\"}}, \"safety_ethics\": {\"extensions\": {\"risk_summary\": \"The model is trained to follow safety policies by default, but its open weights can be modified to bypass refusals or increase harmful capabilities; deployment safeguards remain important.\"}, \"mitigation\": [{\"reference\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.10925\", \"description\": \"Pretraining data was filtered for harmful content, especially hazardous biosecurity knowledge, using CBRN pretraining filters reused from GPT-4o.\"}, {\"reference\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.10925\", \"description\": \"Post-training used deliberative alignment to teach refusals, jailbreak robustness, and adherence to the instruction hierarchy.\"}, {\"reference\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.10925\", \"description\": \"OpenAI conducted scalable capability evaluations and adversarial fine-tuning evaluations for biological/chemical and cyber risks; external Safety Advisory Group review is reported.\"}], \"safety_risk\": [{\"reference\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.10925\", \"description\": \"Open-weight models can be fine-tuned by downstream actors to bypass safety refusals or enhance harmful capabilities.\"}, {\"reference\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.10925\", \"description\": \"The report identifies hallucinations and warns that exposed chain-of-thought can contain hallucinated content or language inconsistent with standard safety policies.\"}, {\"reference\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.10925\", \"description\": \"The default model did not meet the report’s indicative High capability threshold in biological and chemical, cyber, or AI self-improvement tracked categories; adversarially fine-tuned versions were also evaluated.\"}], \"prohibited_use\": [{\"reference\": \"https://github.com/openai/gpt-oss/blob/main/USAGE_POLICY\", \"description\": \"The accompanying gpt-oss usage policy requires users to comply with all applicable law.\"}], \"ethical_considerations\": [{\"reference\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.10925\", \"description\": \"The model is text-only and does not replace a medical professional or serve as a tool for disease diagnosis or treatment.\"}, {\"reference\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.10925\", \"description\": \"The report advises against showing chain-of-thought directly to end users without additional filtering, moderation, or summarization.\"}]}, \"license_policy\": [{\"license\": \"Apache License 2.0\", \"extensions\": {\"kind\": \"declared\", \"source\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.10925\", \"spdx_id\": \"Apache-2.0\", \"scope_note\": \"The model card and official repository declare Apache 2.0 for the released weights and related materials; the repository also supplies a separate usage-policy file.\", \"license_uri\": \"https://github.com/openai/gpt-oss/blob/main/LICENSE\", \"commercial_use\": \"allowed\", \"usage_policy_uri\": \"https://github.com/openai/gpt-oss/blob/main/USAGE_POLICY\"}, \"restrictions\": [\"Redistributions must include a copy of the license.\", \"Modified files must carry prominent notices stating that they were changed.\", \"Retain applicable copyright, patent, trademark, and attribution notices; include NOTICE contents when applicable.\", \"The gpt-oss usage policy requires compliance with all applicable law.\"], \"usage_policy\": \"OpenAI gpt-oss Usage Policy\"}], \"transformation\": {\"input\": [], \"method\": [\"text-only pretraining\", \"large-scale distillation (details undisclosed)\", \"chain-of-thought reinforcement-learning post-training for reasoning and tool use\", \"supervised instruction-hierarchy post-training\", \"MXFP4 post-training quantization of MoE weights\"], \"datasets\": [{\"role\": \"pretraining\", \"dataset\": \"slug:gpt-oss-pretraining-mixture\"}, {\"role\": \"other\", \"dataset\": \"slug:gpt-oss-posttraining-problem-mixture\"}], \"objective\": \"Create an open-weight reasoning model with strong reasoning and agentic tool-use capabilities, while reducing inference memory through MoE and MXFP4 quantization.\", \"timestamp\": \"2025-08-05\", \"extensions\": {\"notes\": \"The report states that pretraining used trillions of text tokens focused on STEM, coding, and general knowledge, with CBRN-related harmful-content filtering. Post-training used a broad range of coding, math, science, and other problems; exact corpus composition, distillation sources, and most training settings are undisclosed. Quantization is reported for MoE weights at MXFP4 (4.25 bits per parameter).\", \"evidence\": [\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.10925\", \"https://openai.com/index/introducing-gpt-oss/\"]}, \"hyperparameters\": null}}, \"draft\": {\"modelId\": \"openai/gpt-oss-120b\", \"modelUrl\": \"https://huggingface.co/openai/gpt-oss-120b\", \"supplier\": \"OpenAI\", \"bomFormat\": null, \"familyKey\": \"gptoss\", \"modelName\": \"gpt-oss-120b\", \"modelRole\": \"DERIVED\", \"namespace\": \"openai\", \"bomVersion\": null, \"familyName\": \"GPT-OSS\", \"packageUrl\": \"pkg:huggingface/openai/gpt-oss-120b\", \"tensorType\": \"MXFP4 for MoE weights\", \"description\": \"Official 120B-class open-weight reasoning checkpoint in the GPT-OSS family, described in OpenAI’s “gpt-oss-120b & gpt-oss-20b Model Card” (arXiv:2508.10925). It is optimized for high-reasoning, general-purpose and agentic use, and its reported training includes pretraining, distillation and reinforcement learning.\", \"detailsJson\": {\"model\": {\"id\": \"openai/gpt-oss-120b\", \"title\": \"openai/gpt-oss-120b\", \"sources\": [\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.10925\", \"https://cdn.openai.com/pdf/419b6906-9da6-406c-a19d-