ass@1\", \"dataset\": \"openai/openai_humaneval\", \"timestamp\": \"2024-11-23\", \"extensions\": {\"reference\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.21783\"}, \"configuration\": {\"notes\": \"Reported as 58.5 ± 7.5; pre-trained 70B result. The paper states that its reported results are for Llama 3.1 models, although it abbreviates the name to Llama 3 in the body.\", \"benchmark\": \"HumanEval\"}}, {\"score\": 81.8, \"metric\": null, \"dataset\": \"slug:squad\", \"timestamp\": \"2024-11-23\", \"extensions\": {\"reference\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.21783\"}, \"configuration\": {\"notes\": \"Reported as 81.8 ± 0.7; pre-trained 70B result. The paper\'s table does not specify the metric in the reported row. The paper states that its reported results are for Llama 3.1 models, although it abbreviates the name to Llama 3 in the body.\", \"benchmark\": \"SQuAD\"}}], \"provenance\": {\"origin\": \"Llama 3.1\", \"evidence\": [\"https://huggingface.co/meta-llama/Llama-3.1-70B\", \"https://huggingface.co/meta-llama/Llama-3.1-70B/blob/main/README.md\", \"https://github.com/meta-llama/llama-models/blob/main/models/sku_list.py\", \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.21783\"], \"provider\": \"Meta\", \"relation\": \"pretrained\", \"extensions\": {\"notes\": \"Official pretrained base checkpoint. The model card describes pretraining on publicly available sources but does not identify the corpus components.\", \"disclosure_status\": \"partially_disclosed\"}}, \"safety_ethics\": {\"extensions\": {\"risk_summary\": \"The model can produce inaccurate, biased, or objectionable responses; the model card recommends application-specific safety testing and tuning before deployment.\"}, \"mitigation\": [{\"reference\": \"https://huggingface.co/meta-llama/Llama-3.1-70B\", \"description\": \"The model card recommends developers perform safety testing and tuning tailored to their applications and deploy necessary safeguards.\"}, {\"reference\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.21783\", \"description\": \"Pretraining data curation includes filtering domains associated with unsafe content, high volumes of personally identifiable information, and adult content.\"}, {\"reference\": \"https://huggingface.co/meta-llama/Llama-3.1-70B\", \"description\": \"Before deployment, developers should conduct application-specific safety testing and tuning.\"}], \"safety_risk\": [{\"reference\": \"https://huggingface.co/meta-llama/Llama-3.1-70B\", \"description\": \"The model card states that outputs may be inaccurate, biased, or otherwise objectionable, and that testing cannot cover every scenario.\"}, {\"reference\": \"https://huggingface.co/meta-llama/Llama-3.1-70B\", \"description\": \"The model may produce inaccurate, biased, or objectionable responses; testing cannot cover every use scenario.\"}, {\"reference\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.21783\", \"description\": \"The report describes filtering unsafe and high-PII web domains during pretraining, but does not claim this eliminates harmful or sensitive content from model outputs.\"}], \"prohibited_use\": [{\"reference\": \"https://huggingface.co/meta-llama/Llama-3.1-70B\", \"description\": \"The Acceptable Use Policy prohibits unlawful or rights-violating uses, harmful conduct, unauthorized professional practice, privacy violations, infringement, malicious code, and specified harmful or deceptive activities.\"}, {\"reference\": \"https://huggingface.co/meta-llama/Llama-3.1-70B\", \"description\": \"The model card also identifies use outside applicable law, the Acceptable Use Policy, or the license—and use in languages beyond those explicitly supported—as out of scope.\"}, {\"reference\": \"https://huggingface.co/meta-llama/Llama-3.1-70B\", \"description\": \"Use must comply with applicable laws and regulations and the Llama 3.1 Acceptable Use Policy, including its prohibited-use terms.\"}], \"ethical_considerations\": [{\"reference\": \"https://huggingface.co/meta-llama/Llama-3.1-70B\", \"description\": \"Developers should evalua